                <pb facs="0559" n="1293" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1293"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 479.—Verbal note.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April 2,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>A pension of 1,200 piastres a month having been granted by iradé of His Imperial
                    Majesty the Sultan to the widow and to the three children of the late Mr. Stupe,
                    American citizen, the ministry of foreign affairs begs of the legation of the
                    United States of America to let the ministry have the name of each one of the
                    children, and to inform it at the same time whether any one among the girls is
                    married already.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
